			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@cferdinandi\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>cferdinandi</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <br>Nothing technically preventing them but there's also the Open Graph protocol (og) which was created at Facebook but is open and used a number of other platforms. </p><p>Google Search also uses a format based on schema.org syntax.</p><p><a href=\"https://ogp.me\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"\">ogp.me</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a></p><p><a href=\"https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/structured-data/article\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">developers.google.com/search/d</span><span class=\"invisible\">ocs/appearance/structured-data/article</span></a></p>",
