			"date": "2023-07-04T17:40:12.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> twitter:card just joins meta name=description and the ten different apple-touch-icon-precomposed things and so on. Simlar to an .htaccess file showing redirects from your URL Schemes Of Times Past; the litany of hidden &lt;head&gt; metadata is like \"we were here\" messages scratched into the walls of Pompeii, or the stone recording that Bybon son of Phola could lift it over his head. Marginalia from monks complaining about the wine in mediaeval manuscripts. A sort of shared cultural history.</p>",
